  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Catastrophe Risk Assessment and Financing Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To provide technical assistance and capital to provide insurance for the Pacific Islands so in future they can protect themselves against natural disasters such as cyclones and Tsunamis thereby reducing their reliance on humanitarian aid. 
The nations of Tonga, Marshall islands, Cook Islands, Vanuatu, and Samoa (625,000 people in total) will benefit from the insurance at the start of the programme</narrative>
  </description>
